Short:        Markdown editor with HTML preview
Author:       André Gewert <agewert@ubergeek.de>
Uploader:     André Gewert <agewert@ubergeek.de>
Type:         text/edit
Version:      1.1
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.2.0
Requires:     AmigaOS 3.2, dev/gui/html_gadget.lha (1.2), AISS (toolbar)
Distribution: Aminet

Kickdown is a Markdown editor for AmigaOS 3.2 with a live HTML preview,
built with ReAction. mdtohtml converts Markdown files to HTML pages from
the Shell. Both use md4c, a fast CommonMark compliant parser written in
C, and understand GitHub flavoured Markdown: tables, strikethrough, task
lists, autolinks and footnotes.

Kickdown
--------
 - editor (texteditor.gadget) and preview (html.gadget) side by side,
   the bar between them adjusts the split
 - syntax highlighting of headings, emphasis, code, quotes, lists, links,
   tables and HTML in the editor, line numbers on request
 - the preview follows half a second after you stop typing and keeps
   its scroll position; editor and preview scroll together
 - headings get anchors, so "#anchor" links and tables of contents
   work; links to other .md files open them in the editor
 - pictures with relative paths are loaded from the document's drawer
 - open, save, save as, export to HTML (with your own page template)
 - cut, copy, paste, undo, redo; text selected in the preview can be
   copied as well
 - find and replace (case sensitive, whole words, backwards, wrap
   around, replace all as one undo step)
 - formatting from the toolbar and the Format menu: heading, bold,
   italic, underline, code, link, image, bulleted, numbered and task
   list, quote; on the selection or the lines, each one undo step
 - toolbar with AISS images (TBIMAGES:), images and text or text only,
   flat or with frames; buttons that would do nothing are ghosted,
   buttons that do not fit into a narrow window are in a drop-down list;
   the formatting buttons can be hidden
 - AppWindow: drop a Markdown icon on the window to open it; iconify
 - splash window while starting (can be switched off)
 - settings window: editor, preview (renderer, TrueType fonts), Markdown
   dialect, charset, page template, highlighting colours, window size
   and position, toolbar; saved as tool types of the Kickdown icon
 - options as tool types or Shell arguments:
   Kickdown [FILE] <name.md> [TEMPLATE <file>] [CHARSET <name>]
            [DIALECT GitHub|CommonMark] [TTF] [NOAUTOREFRESH] [NOSYNC]
            [NOHIGHLIGHT] [LINENUMBERS] [FONTSET Vera|DejaVu|Noto] [SIZE n]
   TTF uses htmlttf.gadget (anti-aliased TrueType fonts) for the preview.

mdtohtml
--------
   mdtohtml [FROM] <file.md> [TO <file.html>] [TEMPLATE <file>]
            [CHARSET <name>] [TITLE <text>] [DIALECT GitHub|CommonMark]

Without FROM the text is read from standard input, without TO the page
goes to standard output. The title defaults to the first heading. The
charset is only written into the page: UTF-8 if the text is valid UTF-8,
otherwise ISO-8859-1. Raw HTML in the text is passed through.

A template is an HTML file with the placeholders $title$, $encoding$ and
$body$, see Template.html.

Installation
------------
Double click Install: it copies Kickdown with the page template and the
example into a drawer of your choice, mdtohtml to C:, the documentation,
and the catalogs of the languages you select to LOCALE:Catalogs. Kickdown
also runs directly from the archive. html.gadget must be installed in
SYS:Classes/Gadgets/ or lie next to Kickdown. Set the default tool of your
Markdown icons to Kickdown to open them with a double click.

Languages
---------
Kickdown speaks English (built in) and German (Catalogs/deutsch). New
translations: Source/catalogs/Kickdown.cd lists all strings, a translation
is a .ct file as for CatComp or FlexCat.

Contents
--------
 Install              Installer script (English/German)
 Kickdown             the editor
 Catalogs/            translations (German)
 C/mdtohtml           the Shell converter
 Example.md           Markdown example
 Template.html        example page template
 Docs/                documentation (English ReadMe.md, German
                      LiesMich.md)
 Icons/               the archive's icons as GlowIcons and NewIcons (and
                      the classic ones); double click UseGlowIcons,
                      UseNewIcons or UseClassic to switch
 Source/              complete source code (C, cross compiled with
                      bebbo's amiga-gcc and NDK 3.2), including md4c

History
-------
1.1 (03.10.2026)
 - printing (Project/Print, Amiga-P, toolbar): to the printer through
   printer.device (graphics, the fonts of the preview; printer unit chosen in
   the window, the resolution of the printer settings), as PostScript to a
   file, PRT:, PS: (TurboPrint) or a device, or as PDF; paper size, margins,
   font and size, page numbers, background colours, page range, copies;
   PostScript level 2 or 1; pictures are compressed (LZW, JPEG files as they
   are, not in level 1); a window shows the progress and can stop it; needs
   html_gadget 1.2; with TurboPrint, Kickdown prints through PostScript level
   2 to PS:
 - new setting (Preview page, tool type FITIMAGES, off by default): big
   pictures are scaled down to the width of the preview and of the
   printed page; needs html_gadget 1.2
 - menu check marks keep their state after iconifying and after changes
   in the settings window
 - "images and text" toolbar: pressed buttons show the AISS selected
   image again
 - settings window: the category list is as wide as its longest entry,
   a bar between list and page adjusts the split
1.0 (03.10.2026)
 - first release

